  "description": "Compile-time twin of Thessera's startup and runtime checks: an aggregate without [AggregateName], a domain event without [EventName], an aggregate whose parameterless constructor is not private, a child entity whose constructor is not internal, an aggregate- or entity-state that names the wrong type as itself, a command handler that touches more than one aggregate or bypasses the unit of work, and raising a retired domain event are a build error instead of a message the first affected host prints at boot, or an exception on the first applied or raised event. Ships no Thessera runtime code - reference it from every host, regardless of which store it selects.",
